      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-03T02:33:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Frank, \n\nThe idea here is that the reclaim reuses the existing `state_t`, so the lock still has the NSM state the client sent when it first acquired it. After the client restarts, its `SM_NOTIFY` carries a new NSM state.\n\nThat won\u0027t match the state on the lock, so `state_nlm_notify()` releases it just like any other lock left over from before the restart.\n\nI can generate some evidence if needed, because I\u0027ve tested that on \u0027next\u0027.",
      "parentUuid": "b5f7b4c3_28ed8259",
